From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Cook <jake@asus-irl-desktop.lawn.gatech.edu>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:01:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: Keep RGxx3 sdmmc1 IO rails on in
 suspend

The second SD slot (sdmmc1) on the RGxx3 family keeps its card powered
across suspend (vmmc is vcc_3v3, always-on and on-in-suspend) while both
rails that reference its bus are switched off: vcc_1v8 (LDO7, VCCIO4 -
the IO domain the SDMMC1 pads and their card-detect GPIO2_B2 sit in) and
vcc1v8_dvp (LDO8, what the node names as vqmmc). Every suspend therefore
leaves a live card on an unpowered bus and lets the card-detect input
float; on resume the pads come back up against the card, the latched
card-detect edge triggers a rescan, and because vmmc can never be cycled
a card that was upset by the glitch stays unusable until it is physically
reinserted. Users see the games card vanish after resume, sometimes
with a corrupted exFAT filesystem. The boot slot is unaffected: its pads
are in VCCIO3 (vccio_sd) and its card-detect is in the always-on PMU IO
domain.

Keep both rails at 1.8V through suspend so the bus and card-detect stay
referenced for as long as the card is powered.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-anbernic-rgxx3.dtsi | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-anbernic-rgxx3.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-anbernic-rgxx3.dtsi
@@ -346,7 +346,8 @@
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
 				regulator-name = "vcc_1v8";
 				regulator-state-mem {
-					regulator-off-in-suspend;
+					regulator-on-in-suspend;
+					regulator-suspend-microvolt = <1800000>;
 				};
 			};
 
@@ -356,7 +357,8 @@
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
 				regulator-name = "vcc1v8_dvp";
 				regulator-state-mem {
-					regulator-off-in-suspend;
+					regulator-on-in-suspend;
+					regulator-suspend-microvolt = <1800000>;
 				};
 			};
 
